WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.032
DATE_TRUNC changes the analytical grain of a timestamp.

00:00:04.032 --> 00:00:09.067
A timestamp can be truncated to day, week, month, quarter, or other levels.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:14.207
The returned value represents the start of that period.

00:00:14.207 --> 00:00:20.642
This makes DATE_TRUNC especially useful for GROUP BY because all timestamps in the same period receive the

00:00:20.642 --> 00:00:25.922
same bucket value. Choose temporal types based on meaning.

00:00:25.922 --> 00:00:29.652
DATE is for calendar dates without time of day.

00:00:29.652 --> 00:00:34.727
TIMESTAMP stores a date and time without a time-zone interpretation.

00:00:34.727 --> 00:00:41.657
TIMESTAMPTZ represents an instant in time and is usually safer for events that cross regions or

00:00:41.657 --> 00:00:43.446
daylight-saving changes.
